      "category": "evidenceCoverage",
      "researchLocation": "synthesisInput: Facts 6–7; Unknowns",
      "problem": "The projection records the AI-first and potentially AI-only labels but omits the source’s explanation of what AI-first is intended to mean, and that AI-only’s operational meaning is undefined. Because this projection is meant to support an account of the company’s identity, those qualifications matter to how the labels may be interpreted.",
      "sourceQuote": "NuEbyon\u0019s intended positioning is that of a company built around AI rather than a conventional software company that adds AI as an additional feature.\n\nThis ambition has two related dimensions.\n\nFirst, AI is central to the products NuEbyon intends to build. The products should use AI as a fundamental capability to accomplish useful work.\n\nSecond, the company itself is intended to operate in an AI-first manner, using AI as a central part of how products are conceived, developed, and operated.\n\nThe broader AI-only ambition expresses a stronger version of this positioning, but its precise operational meaning has not yet been defined in the available source material.",
      "constraint": "Preserve the source’s intended meaning of AI-first and state that AI-only’s operational meaning remains undefined; do not imply that the company already operates entirely through AI or without human involvement."
    },
    {
      "category": "evidenceCoverage",
      "researchLocation": "synthesisInput: Unknowns 3",
      "problem": "The projection limits its effectiveness caveat to the broader portfolio. The source also explicitly says the company’s strategic premise is not evidence that identified needs have been validated or that proposed solutions have demonstrated effectiveness. Omitting that broader limit could leave the core product direction open to being represented as validated or effective when the source does not support that conclusion.",
      "sourceQuote": "This is the strategic premise behind the company, not a claim that every identified need has already been validated or that the proposed solutions have demonstrated their effectiveness.",
      "constraint": "Retain the source’s qualification that identified needs are not necessarily validated and proposed solutions are not shown here to be effective; do not assert a specific validation or effectiveness outcome."
    }
  ]
}
